        {
          "subsection_id": "volkmann_retractor_subsection_2",
          "subsection_title": "1. Introduction and identification",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "volkmann_retractor_group_2",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A Volkmann retractor, also called a rake retractor, is a handheld surgical instrument used to retract skin and superficial soft tissues to improve exposure of the operative field."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Its defining feature is a rake-like working end with multiple prongs. Depending on the design, the prongs may be sharp or blunt."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "OSCE identification card"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Name: Volkmann retractor (rake retractor)"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Classification: Handheld tissue retractor"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Primary function: Retracting skin and superficial soft tissues."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Characteristic feature: A rake-like end with multiple projecting prongs."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Mechanism: Manually held; the standard pattern is not self-retaining."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "OSCE identification clue: If you see several short prongs arranged like a rake at the end of a handle, think of a Volkmann retractor."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "volkmann_retractor_subsection_3",
          "subsection_title": "2. Parts and labelling",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "volkmann_retractor_group_3",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/volkmann_retractor_02.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Part",
                    "Description and function"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Handle",
                      "Provides a grip for manual control."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Shaft",
                      "Connects the handle to the working end."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Neck or curved section",
                      "Positions the prongs at the required angle to the handle."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Rake head",
                      "The working end carrying multiple prongs."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Prongs",
                      "Engage and retract tissue."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Prong tips",
                      "May be sharp or blunt, depending on the model."
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The number of prongs, their curvature and their sharpness vary by model. In an OSCE, describe the actual instrument rather than assuming every Volkmann has the same configuration."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "volkmann_retractor_subsection_4",
          "subsection_title": "3. Classification and types",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "volkmann_retractor_group_4",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/volkmann_retractor_03.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A. Three-pronged Volkmann retractor"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Has three projecting prongs. Used for localized retraction of skin and superficial tissues."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/volkmann_retractor_04.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "B. Four-pronged Volkmann retractor"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Has four prongs, allowing engagement of a broader area than some three-pronged patterns."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/volkmann_retractor_05.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "C. Blunt-pronged pattern"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Has rounded or blunt tips intended to reduce penetration of tissue, although pressure-related injury remains possible."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/volkmann_retractor_06.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "D. Sharp-pronged pattern"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Has pointed tips that engage the tissue more firmly. Requires particular care to prevent puncture or tearing."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "volkmann_retractor_subsection_5",
          "subsection_title": "4. Uses and clinical applications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "volkmann_retractor_group_5",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The Volkmann retractor is primarily used for superficial tissue retraction."
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Use",
                    "Explanation"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Skin retraction",
                      "Holds skin edges apart to improve exposure."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Superficial wound exposure",
                      "Retracts superficial tissues during dissection."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Minor surgery",
                      "Provides localized retraction around a small incision."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Orthopaedic procedures",
                      "May help retract superficial soft tissues over an operative site."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Plastic surgery",
                      "Assists with exposure during selected superficial procedures."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Wound closure",
                      "Helps expose wound edges during appropriate suturing procedures."
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "volkmann_retractor_group_6",
              "group_title": "Procedures where it may be used",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Excision of superficial lesions.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Selected orthopaedic operations.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Minor surgical procedures.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Plastic and reconstructive surgery.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Selected general surgical procedures involving superficial dissection.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Important distinction: The Volkmann retractor is not primarily designed for deep abdominal organ retraction. A broad, long-curved retractor such as a Deaver is generally more suitable when deep cavity retraction is required."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "volkmann_retractor_subsection_6",
          "subsection_title": "5. Advantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "volkmann_retractor_group_7",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Secure engagement: Multiple prongs can maintain contact with superficial tissue.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "1."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Good localized exposure: Useful for retracting skin and superficial wound edges.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "2."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Simple design: Easy to manipulate and inspect.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "3."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Different prong configurations: Sharp or blunt tips accommodate different retraction requirements.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "4."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Immediate adjustment: The operator can change the angle and traction manually.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "5."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Reusable designs: Stainless-steel models can be reprocessed using validated procedures.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "6."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "volkmann_retractor_subsection_7",
          "subsection_title": "6. Disadvantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "volkmann_retractor_group_8",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "list",
                  "items": [
                    {
                      "text": "Sharp prongs may puncture or tear tissue.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "1."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Retraction force is concentrated at several small contact points.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "2."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Excessive pulling can damage skin and superficial soft tissues.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "3."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "It must be held manually, which may cause operator fatigue.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "4."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "It is unsuitable for substantial deep-cavity retraction.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "5."
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Prongs may catch on tissue or dressings during placement or removal.",
                      "level": 0,
                      "label": "6."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "volkmann_retractor_subsection_8",
          "subsection_title": "7. Complications of improper use",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "volkmann_retractor_group_9",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Complication",
                    "Mechanism",
                    "Prevention"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Skin puncture",
                      "Sharp prongs penetrate tissue",
                      "Use the appropriate prong type and controlled placement."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Tissue tearing",
                      "Excessive traction or poor positioning",
                      "Apply gentle traction and avoid levering."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Bleeding",
                      "Injury to superficial blood vessels",
                      "Retract under direct vision."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Pressure injury",
                      "Excessive or prolonged force",
                      "Reassess the retraction and reposition as needed."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Wound-edge damage",
                      "Prongs catch or pull through tissue",
                      "Release the instrument carefully."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Accidental staff injury",
                      "Contact with sharp prongs",
                      "Maintain awareness of the working end."
                    ]
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "High-yield point: The rake-like design is the main identification feature, but the prongs also create a potential risk of puncture injury and tissue tearing."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "volkmann_retractor_subsection_9",
          "subsection_title": "8. Principles of proper handling",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "volkmann_retractor_group_10",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/volkmann_retractor_07.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 1 — Inspect the prongs"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Check for bent, damaged or misaligned tips and confirm that the instrument is clean and sterile."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/volkmann_retractor_08.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 2 — Position appropriately"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Engage the intended superficial tissue carefully, avoiding vulnerable structures and unnecessary penetration."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/volkmann_retractor_09.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 3 — Apply controlled traction"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Use only the force required for exposure. Avoid excessive pulling or allowing the prongs to cut through the tissue."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/volkmann_retractor_10.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Step 4 — Release and reprocess"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Remove the instrument carefully, protecting the prongs, then clean and sterilize it according to the manufacturer's instructions and validated protocol."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
